---
description: A review finding is about the pull request head it was written on
alwaysApply: true
---

# Review findings

A comment on a pull request is about that pull request's head. Read it against that head before calling the pull request ready to merge.

A finding that asks for a change is still open when that head does not contain the change. Say so. A later pull request stacked above the head does not resolve it.

A finding that is tried and not adopted is answered with the measurement or the reason, on the pull request it was written on (`.cursor/rules/bench.mdc`).

Before acting on a finding or declining it, check its claim against the code of that head: run the reproduction, or read the lines it names. A finding can be right about the reader's difficulty and wrong about the fact.

A finding that asks to change a decision the owner made is not declined by citing the rule that records the decision. Reply with what the decision was and what the finding shows, and ask the owner (`.cursor/rules/consent.mdc`).

Before calling a PR ready, and whenever the owner asks for the next step, read the reviews and inline comments of every open PR (`gh pr view <n> --json reviews,comments` and `gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/<n>/comments`).

```text
# BAD
The ref-lifetime check is missing. A later pull request sits on this head, so merge.

# GOOD
The ref-lifetime check is not in this head. The finding stays open.
```
